    pr_ref:  # 6c79
    description: "F65.A4 (blind severity 2/Minor). Two separate modules expose a parameter literally named hub_threshold with different semantics and different defaults: the centrality-ranking module uses it for in-degree log-saturation in scoring (default 100), while the slice module uses it for traversal hub-pruning (default 50). They share no definition; the two distinct defaults confirm they are independent machinery. A slice feature's query.hub_threshold echo (50) and a centrality config's hub_threshold (100) are the same key name for unrelated knobs. A consumer who carries a value or mental model from one mechanism to the other configures the wrong behavior (mis-tuning). No emitted value is corrupted; the hazard is conceptual and invites configuration errors. Fix: distinct self-descriptive names (or a documented disambiguation) so a consumer reading 'hub_threshold' knows which mechanism and which default applies. filed via tranch 04 (methodology-comparability run, reused tranch-03 substrate sha a32c4a31)."  # 6c79
    fields: {}  # 6c79
